        "comments": "The assembly ddHypMacu1.hap1.1 is based on 61x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The species looks to be tetraploid (4n=32). We can clearly see 3 chromosomes which seem to recombine and one univalent in each set of 4 chromosomes. Some haplotype inversions could be observed on: Chromosome 1_HAP3 6.35 Mbp - 12.83 Mbp, Chromosome 1_HAP4 7.17 Mbp - 14.47 Mbp Chromosome 2_HAP2 0.04 Mbp - 15.70 Mbp, Chromosome 2_HAP3 0.20 Mbp - 16.93 Mbp, Chromosome 2_HAP4 0.00 Mbp - 17.09 Mbp, Chromosome 2_HAP3 2.58 Mbp - 6.97 Mbp, Chromosome 2_HAP4 2.62 Mbp - 8.28 Mbp Chromosome 3_HAP1 18.65 Mbp - 26.19 Mbp, Chromosome 3_HAP2 35.21 Mbp - 43.62 Mbp, Chromosome 3_HAP3 28.04 Mbp - 34.02 Mbp, Chromosome 3_HAP4 40.62 Mbp - 45.42 Mbp Chromosome 4_HAP1 20.41 Mbp - 28.49 Mbp, Chromosome 4_HAP2 19.68 Mbp - 30.46 Mbp, Chromosome 4_HAP3 19.84 Mbp - 25.66 Mbp, Chromosome 4_HAP4 18.57 Mbp - 23.94 Mbp Chromosome 5_HAP3 18.24 Mbp - 19.35 Mbp, Chromosome 5_HAP4 15.70 Mbp - 17.09 Mbp Chromosome 6_HAP1 16.81 Mbp - 28.20 Mbp, Chromosome 6_HAP2 15.95 Mbp - 25.70 Mbp, Chromosome 6_HAP3 16.72 Mbp - 26.93 Mbp, Chromosome 6_HAP4 14.59 Mbp - 28.08 Mbp Chromosome 7_HAP1 20.50 Mbp - 29.39 Mbp, Chromosome 7_HAP2 18.61 Mbp - 26.81 Mbp, Chromosome 7_HAP3 19.14 Mbp - 26.15 Mbp, Chromosome 7_HAP4 8.12 Mbp - 12.95 Mbp. Chromosome 7_HAP4 looks collapsed. Chromosome 8_HAP3 14.68 Mbp - 18.57 Mbp, Chromosome 8_HAP4 9.02 Mbp - 17.59 Mbp One translocation was observed between Chromosomes 1 and 3: SUPER_1_HAP1 0.00 Mbp - 21.23 Mbp and SUPER_3 start to 18.77 Mbp in HAP2, HAP3 and HAP4.",
